  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "Done. The cause was float math in `billing/totals.py`. Prices and tax were converted with `float()` and then rounded with `round()`. Values that should land exactly on a half cent, like `1.005`, came out as `1.00499999…`. They rounded down, and Python's `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even number. Either way the line was off by one cent, and the invoice `TOTAL` inherited the error.\n\nI switched `line_total_cents` to `Decimal` arithmetic with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so half cents round up. I also added a regression test, `test_half_cent_rounds_up`.\n\nAll 7 tests pass. With the old `totals.py` restored, the suite fails (1 failure), so the new test does catch the bug.\n\nI didn't run the CSV report on real data, and I assumed half-cents should round up. If your billing rules say otherwise (for example, banker's rounding), tell me and I'll change the rounding mode.",
